Description: Drop -lbnetapi and -lnetservices from the link line
 On V\OS the network kit (BNet* sockets) and netservices (BUrlRequest,
 BUrlProtocolListener, BHttpRequest, BJson, ...) are compiled into libbe;
 there is no separate libbnetapi or libnetservices to link against, and
 libbe is already in LIBS. Upstream still names the two legacy
 libraries, which fails with:
   /usr/bin/ld: cannot find -lbnetapi: No such file or directory
   /usr/bin/ld: cannot find -lnetservices: No such file or directory
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Origin: V\OS port of HaikuArchives/Weather

--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@
 #	- 	if your library does not follow the standard library naming scheme,
 #		you need to specify the path to the library and it's name.
 #		(e.g. for mylib.a, specify "mylib.a" or "path/mylib.a")
-LIBS = be bnetapi localestub translation netservices shared $(STDCPPLIBS)
+LIBS = be localestub translation shared $(STDCPPLIBS)
 
 #	Specify additional paths to directories following the standard libXXX.so
 #	or libXXX.a naming scheme. You can specify full paths or paths relative
